 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A foot of rain and four deaths. What did Isaias leave behind?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Isaias came ashore near Destin, Florida, on Friday night as a Category 2 hurricane. Within hours it weakened to a post-tropical cyclone, but the damage was done. Fox Weather reports at least four deaths in Florida and Alabama."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Falling trees killed two people in Alabama and one in Florida, local authorities said. Another man died from generator fumes in his garage. Reports say nearly 396,000 customers across the Florida Panhandle and southern Alabama were still without power early Sunday."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Rain was the other blow. Gauges recorded almost thirteen inches in Bellwood, Alabama, and more than twelve in parts of Florida. A flash flood emergency covered Destin and Fort Walton Beach. The storm has since moved north toward the Appalachians."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the death toll rise in the coming days? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
